{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B4MS6uD7kJ733dg221bTo1","type":"tool_result","content":"== GOAL 1 — the daemon and the thin client exist at all\nFAIL  1a no rabadon-gated binary — the persistent daemon is not built\n      this is the whole speed half of R7; without it GOALs 2 and 3 measure nothing\nFAIL  1b no daemon source that binds AF_UNIX and listens\n      searched native/gated.cpp, native/daemon.cpp, native/gated.h\nFAIL  1c nothing in the gate reaches for a daemon socket — there is no thin client\n\n== GOAL 2 — with the daemon up, the gate's median is under 1 ms (in-process)\nFAIL  2a the daemon cannot be started — it does not exist\nFAIL  2b the < 1 ms median was NOT measured: no daemon to measure with\n      ceiling is 1000 us in-process; the instrument is the R1.3 probe (header)\nFAIL  2c the residual length dependence was NOT re-measured under the daemon\n      R1.3 closed at 3.5-4.9% under a 10% ceiling with process spawn IN the\n      denominator; the daemon removes spawn, so the same absolute cost reads as\n      a LARGER percentage. The plan requires R7 to re-read it. Unread today.\n\n== GOAL 3 — with the daemon down, behaviour is byte-identical to today\nFAIL  3a exit codes with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED — there is no client path to compare\nFAIL  3b ledger lines with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED\nFAIL  3c refusals with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED\n      with no client, 'the daemon is down' is indistinguishable from today by\n      construction, and a comparison that cannot fail is not evidence\n\n== GOAL 4 — the harness is named, exactly, with its commit\nPASS  4a reports/R7/ exists\nPASS  4b the harness is named by full repo: SWE-bench/SWE-smith\nPASS  4c the harness commit hash is pinned (40 hex)\nFAIL  4d the .git-cleaning / egress-closing preparation is not recorded (with its best-effort label)\n\n== GOAL 5 — the raw run lands here, and can be re-run\nFAIL  5a no non-empty *.jsonl under reports/R7/ — a summary is not the evidence\nFAIL  5b no JSONL to check for two arms\nFAIL  5c bench/reproduce.sh exists but says nothing about R7's two-armed run\n\n== GOAL 6 — the five numbers, each of them, from the raw data\nFAIL  6a no held-out fix rate in the raw data (field 'heldout_pass' per task, both arms)\n      the agent's own test does not count — that is the metric it is optimising\nFAIL  6b token totals are missing from the raw data\nFAIL  6c human intervention counts are missing from the raw data","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cd1d3b8-0ab4-436c-a096-b92b12ed0757","uuid":"1924e8b4-3ead-4f20-8d74-2f754c73dcec","timestamp":"2026-08-24T10:37:00.396Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"== GOAL 1 — the daemon and the thin client exist at all\nFAIL  1a no rabadon-gated binary — the persistent daemon is not built\n      this is the whole speed half of R7; without it GOALs 2 and 3 measure nothing\nFAIL  1b no daemon source that binds AF_UNIX and listens\n      searched native/gated.cpp, native/daemon.cpp, native/gated.h\nFAIL  1c nothing in the gate reaches for a daemon socket — there is no thin client\n\n== GOAL 2 — with the daemon up, the gate's median is under 1 ms (in-process)\nFAIL  2a the daemon cannot be started — it does not exist\nFAIL  2b the < 1 ms median was NOT measured: no daemon to measure with\n      ceiling is 1000 us in-process; the instrument is the R1.3 probe (header)\nFAIL  2c the residual length dependence was NOT re-measured under the daemon\n      R1.3 closed at 3.5-4.9% under a 10% ceiling with process spawn IN the\n      denominator; the daemon removes spawn, so the same absolute cost reads as\n      a LARGER percentage. The plan requires R7 to re-read it. Unread today.\n\n== GOAL 3 — with the daemon down, behaviour is byte-identical to today\nFAIL  3a exit codes with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED — there is no client path to compare\nFAIL  3b ledger lines with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED\nFAIL  3c refusals with the daemon down are UNCOMPARED\n      with no client, 'the daemon is down' is indistinguishable from today by\n      construction, and a comparison that cannot fail is not evidence\n\n== GOAL 4 — the harness is named, exactly, with its commit\nPASS  4a reports/R7/ exists\nPASS  4b the harness is named by full repo: SWE-bench/SWE-smith\nPASS  4c the harness commit hash is pinned (40 hex)\nFAIL  4d the .git-cleaning / egress-closing preparation is not recorded (with its best-effort label)\n\n== GOAL 5 — the raw run lands here, and can be re-run\nFAIL  5a no non-empty *.jsonl under reports/R7/ — a summary is not the evidence\nFAIL  5b no JSONL to check for two arms\nFAIL  5c bench/reproduce.sh exists but says nothing about R7's two-armed run\n\n== GOAL 6 — the five numbers, each of them, from the raw data\nFAIL  6a no held-out fix rate in the raw data (field 'heldout_pass' per task, both arms)\n      the agent's own test does not count — that is the metric it is optimising\nFAIL  6b token totals are missing from the raw data\nFAIL  6c human intervention counts are missing from the raw data","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
