ifferent cwd?\n\n5. native/gate.cpp around lines 700-760: the existing open_sock() AF_UNIX CLIENT (fan-out to `rabadon watch`). Show me its exact code, how sockPath is computed (line 2718 area), and how failure is handled.\n\n6. What startup work is expensive (things a daemon would do once): any large table/regex/fixture construction, file loads, at namespace scope or early in main. Name them with lines and rough size.\n\nReturn a compressed structured report, max ~60 lines, all with file:line. Do not modify anything."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2098,"cache_read_input_tokens":77857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2098},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cd1d3b8-0ab4-436c-a096-b92b12ed0757","uuid":"95215409-56b7-431e-9ee5-0e4d890fd2f5","request_id":"req_011CeMRkd49PTvuP1eB2vUrp"}
