{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J6fzYSfXCFNiMjqbs2Yexf","type":"tool_result","content":"2705\t  // rabadon home (spool/socket) — env override mirrors core/bus.mjs\n2706\t  const string rdir = rabadon_home();\n2707\t  mkdir(rdir.c_str(), 0755);\n2708\t  mkdir((rdir + \"/spool\").c_str(), 0755);\n2709\t\n2710\t  // project name = basename(cwd)\n2711\t  size_t cs = cwd.rfind('/');\n2712\t  const string project = cs == string::npos ? cwd : cwd.substr(cs + 1);\n2713\t\n2714\t  char day[16]; { time_t t = time(nullptr); struct tm tmv; gmtime_r(&t, &tmv); strftime(day, 16, \"%Y-%m-%d\", &tmv); }\n2715\t\n2716\t  Emitter em;\n2717\t  em.spoolPath = rdir + \"/spool/\" + day + \".jsonl\";\n2718\t  em.sockPath = rdir + \"/rabadon.sock\";\n2719\t  em.pipe = project + \":session\";\n2720\t  em.runId = \"ng-\" + std::to_string(now_ms() % 100000000) + \"-\" + std::to_string(getpid());\n2721\t  em.call = toolUseId;   // read at the top of main and, until now, used only to dedupe twin deliveries\n2722\t  em.sess = sid;\n2723\t  em.drill = sid.rfind(\"fleet-\", 0) == 0 || sid.rfind(\"doctor-\", 0) == 0 || sid.rfind(\"drill-\", 0) == 0;\n2724\t  { const char* de = getenv(\"RABADON_DRILL\"); if (de && strcmp(de, \"1\") == 0) em.drill = true; }\n2725\t  em.open_sock();\n2726\t\n2727\t  // one state file, one owner. the old parallel state-native-*.txt store is\n2728\t  // retired — removed on sight so no stale twin survives the migration.\n2729\t  mkdir((cwd + \"/.rabadon\").c_str(), 0755);\n2730\t  const string sidLegacy = sid.empty() ? \"default\" : sid.substr(0, 16);\n2731\t  unlink((cwd + \"/.rabadon/state-native-\" + sidLegacy + \".txt\").c_str());\n2732\t  State stt;\n2733\t  StateFlushGuard stt_flush(stt);   // every exit path, including exit(): see above\n2734\t  stt.path = cwd + \"/.rabadon/state.json\";\n2735\t  stt.sessDir = cwd + \"/.rabadon/sessions\";\n2736\t  stt.sessKey = session_key(sid);\n2737\t  stt.legacyKey = sidLegacy;\n2738\t  stt.load();\n2739\t  Sess& ss = stt.session();\n2740\t\n2741\t  // twin-delivery dedupe (same law as the node gate): tool events carry a\n2742\t  // unique tool_use_id; non-tool events (Stop/SessionStart/prompt) dedupe on\n2743\t  // a 2s time bucket, which only ever collides with a genuine twin.\n2744\t  //\n2745\t  // A TIME BUCKET IS NOT AN IDENTITY, AND FOR TOOL EVENTS IT WAS A SILENT\n2746\t  // SKIP. The condition used to read `hook != \"PreToolUse\"`, which sent\n2747\t  // PostToolUse — a tool event — down the bucket branch whenever the agent\n2748\t  // sent no tool_use_id. Two genuinely different edits landing in the same\n2749\t  // two seconds then produced ONE supervised event: the second returned 0\n2750\t  // here, before the branch that starts the project's own check, so no check\n2751\t  // ran and a red base could never clear itself. Measured, 3 runs each, two\n2752\t  // edits 300ms apart: same bucket -> the suite ran 1 time and the verdict\n2753\t  // stayed red; across a boundary -> it ran 2 times and went green. The\n2754\t  // recovery half of Promise 2 was failing on exactly this."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNJNRkZewzBF62my6wyhvM","session_id":"5cd1d3b8-0ab4-436c-a096-b92b12ed0757","uuid":"a2845bd5-b4f3-4337-8d63-da05394ca9aa","timestamp":"2026-08-24T10:38:22.222Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map gate.cpp hook path for daemon"}
