{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCygMezmV1ob1KbRmFbfDo","type":"tool_result","content":"632\tstatic string ledger_line(const string& ev, const string& extraJson) {\n633\t  const string rdir = rabadon_home();\n634\t  mkdir(rdir.c_str(), 0755);\n635\t  mkdir((rdir + \"/spool\").c_str(), 0755);\n636\t  char day[16];\n637\t  { time_t t = time(nullptr); struct tm tmv; gmtime_r(&t, &tmv); strftime(day, 16, \"%Y-%m-%d\", &tmv); }\n638\t  const char* who = getenv(\"USER\");\n639\t  string body = \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"seq\\\":1,\\\"ts\\\":\" + std::to_string(now_ms()) +\n640\t    \",\\\"run\\\":\\\"cli-\" + std::to_string(getpid()) + \"\\\",\\\"pipe\\\":\\\"\" +\n641\t    json_escape(string(who ? who : \"cli\")) + \":cli\\\",\\\"ev\\\":\\\"\" + ev + \"\\\"\" +\n642\t    (extraJson.empty() ? \"\" : \",\" + extraJson);\n643\t  // rbchain::append takes an OPEN body: it appends `,\"prev\":\"...\"}` itself, so\n644\t  // closing the object here produced two JSON documents on one line and a chain\n645\t  // the audit correctly called broken.\n646\t  return rbchain::append(rdir + \"/spool/\" + string(day) + \".jsonl\", body);\n647\t}\n648\t\n649\t// SUPERVISION THAT WENT AWAY WITHOUT SAYING SO.\n650\t//\n651\t// `rabadon --off` writes a MODE line, and that was taken to mean mode changes\n652\t// are on the chain. They are not. The switch IS a file, `<rabadon home>/enabled`,\n653\t// and `rm` on that file is the same change with none of the record: measured in\n654\t// an isolated lab, enforce refused `git push --force origin main` with exit 2,\n655\t// the file was removed with rm, the identical command returned exit 0, and the\n656\t// MODE count on the ledger went from 1 to 1. The comment at the toggle already\n657\t// says supervision going away is the most consequential thing anybody does to\n658\t// this tool. It was still the one thing that could happen silently.\n659\t//\n660\t// So the mode is not trusted to announce itself: it is COMPARED, on every hook\n661\t// invocation, against the last mode this machine recorded. A difference with no\n662\t// MODE line between them is written down as one, marked out-of-band, naming both\n663\t// ends. This does not stop the removal — an operator who owns the disk owns the\n664\t// switch, and pretending otherwise would be the lie this tool exists to refuse —\n665\t// it makes the removal leave a mark on the same hash-chained ledger as the\n666\t// refusals it silenced.\n667\t//\n668\t// The marker file lives beside the switch and is written only when the mode\n669\t// actually differs, so the hot path pays one small read and nothing else.\n670\t//\n671\t// After the collapse there is no second copy to compare against, so the\n672\t// comparison is made against the ledger itself — the last MODE line rabadon\n673\t// wrote. That was always the record this existed to produce; mode.last was a\n674\t// shadow of it. The spool is already open on this path, so this costs one\n675\t// backward read of one file, and only on days a MODE line exists.\n676\tstatic void note_mode(const string& now) {\n677\t  const string rdir = rabadon_home();\n678\t  const string was = last_ledger_mode();\n679\t  if (was == now) return;\n680\t  // A machine that has never recorded a mode is not a machine whose supervision\n681\t  // changed. Recording the first observation as a transition would put a fake\n682\t  // MODE line on every fresh install.\n683\t  if (!was.empty())\n684\t    ledger_line(\"MODE\", \"\\\"from\\\":\\\"\" + json_escape(was) + \"\\\",\\\"to\\\":\\\"\" +\n685\t                        json_escape(now) + \"\\\",\\\"outOfBand\\\":true\");\n686\t  (void)rdir;\n687\t}\n688\t\n689\tstruct Emitter {\n690\t  string spoolPath, sockPath, runId, pipe;\n691\t  // Who this event belongs to. Both answers were already in the gate's hands"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNJNRkZewzBF62my6wyhvM","session_id":"5cd1d3b8-0ab4-436c-a096-b92b12ed0757","uuid":"4a0ee8d6-9be3-4b09-8ed5-68ac6a7805fb","timestamp":"2026-08-24T10:38:33.880Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map gate.cpp hook path for daemon"}
