{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G41mPNjDtCcTRXDXsGFvtg","type":"tool_result","content":"219:// The two model names below were compiled in: the drift judge always spoke to\n473:// edge of it. The compiled baseline was never affected because it resolves paths\n751:// The rule engine itself is rules.h. `rabadon exec` compiles the same header,\n754:using rbrules::parse_rules;\n1754:// Default is claude-haiku-4-5, the name that used to be compiled in here.\n1791:  \"  --lint [dir] compile every guard.json pattern and flag unknown keys, so a\\n\"\n2160:  // BLOCK. Lint compiles every pattern and flags unknown top-level keys, exit\n2192:    // every deny/match pattern must compile\n2195:      for (const auto& r : parse_rules(g, section, patKey, empty)) {\n2196:        try { std::regex re(r.pattern); (void)re; }\n2207:    // and a why, and reads as enforced; parse_rules drops it for having no\n2245:        // present-but-empty counts as absent: parse_rules drops an empty\n2260:    // lint called that guard valid, because the rule compiled and it fired.\n2332:            fprintf(stderr, \"              the rule is dead: it compiles, it reads correctly, and no %s reaches it\\n\",\n3475:        std::regex fc(\"\\\\bfail(?:ed|ures)?\\\\s*[:= ]\\\\s*(\\\\d+)\", std::regex::ECMAScript | std::regex::icase);\n3476:        if (std::regex_search(out, m, fc)) passed = (atoll(m[1].str().c_str()) == 0);\n3503:        static const std::regex zeroCount(\n3506:            std::regex::ECMAScript | std::regex::icase);\n3507:        declaredZeroFailures = std::regex_search(out, zeroCount);\n3508:        evid = std::regex_replace(out, zeroCount, \" \");\n3668:            // validate the rule regex compiles; install into bash (deny) or\n3677:            // the rule's regex is JSON-escaped in patRaw; unescape for compile test\n3679:            bool compiles = false;\n3680:            if (target) { try { std::regex re(patUnescaped, std::regex::ECMAScript | std::regex::icase); compiles = true; (void)re; } catch (...) { compiles = false; } }\n3696:            if (target && compiles) {\n3715:            if (target && compiles && !provenLive) {\n3721:            if (target && compiles && provenLive) {\n3893:    const size_t nb = parse_rules(guardRaw, \"bash\", \"deny\", disabled).size();\n3894:    const size_t np = parse_rules(guardRaw, \"protectedPaths\", \"match\", disabled).size();\n4129:  // reason. The baseline is the backstop underneath: three laws compiled into","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNJNRkZewzBF62my6wyhvM","session_id":"5cd1d3b8-0ab4-436c-a096-b92b12ed0757","uuid":"d35bd8a0-aa3c-44de-a15a-a503401e7944","timestamp":"2026-08-24T10:38:43.382Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Map gate.cpp hook path for daemon"}
