_code(), line 72: `g_mode == MODE_ENFORCE ? 2 : 0`)\n\n**Stdout JSON shapes:**\n- Refuse (Cursor): `{\"permission\":\"deny\",\"user_message\":\"...\",\"agent_message\":\"...\"}`\n- Allow with injection: `{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"additionalContext\":\"...\"}}`\n- Allow without injection: empty stdout, exit 0\n\n---\n\n### 3. CRITICAL: What the judgment depends on (per-request vs. cached)\n\n**PER-REQUEST INPUTS (CANNOT be cached across requests):**\n- `cwd` (current working directory) — **line 2567-2568**, fallback to PWD env\n- `toolName`, `command`, `filePath` — from stdin event\n- `sessionId` (sid) — from stdin event\n- `hook` type — from stdin event\n- **Environment variable: RABADON_MODE** (line 2600) — can change per-shell\n- **Environment variable: RABADON_OFF** (line 2582) — can change per-command\n- **Per-project state files:**\n  - `.rabadon/off` (line 2584)\n  - `.rabadon/on` (line 2620)\n  - `.rabadon/mode` (line 2614)\n  - `.rabadon/state.json` (line 2734) — session state (moves, test verdicts, diagnosis pending, etc.)\n  - `.rabadon/sessions/*.json` (line 2735-2738) — session-specific data, loaded via `stt.load()`\n  - `.rabadon/net.json` (line 4350) — for red-base check command\n  - `.rabadon/budget.json` (line 4081) — budget cap\n  - Transcript file at `E.transcriptPath` (line 4088) — for budget token counting\n\n**POTENTIALLY CACHEABLE (but need per-cwd tree walk):**\n- `.rabadon/guard.json` — the rule set (line 2780) — **BUT** guard_path_for() walks the directory tree (line 2779), so the **file location is per-project**, and guard.json can change mid-session\n- **disabled[] rules** (line 2781) — derived from guard.json parse\n\n**ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES READ (per-request or startup):**\n- **RABADON_OFF** (line 2582) — per-request kill switch\n- **RABADON_MODE** (line 2600) — per-request mode override\n- **PWD** (line 2568) — per-request if cwd empty\n- **HOME** (line 489 in guard_path_for) — used once for home bound\n- **RABADON_DIR** (line 169, rbpath::rabadon_dir() in rbpath.h) — machine home\n- **RABADON_DRILL** (line 2724) — per-event drill flag\n- **RABADON_WALK_CAP** (line 3297) — cap on tree walk\n- **RABADON_JUDGE** (line 3159) — judge model selection\n- **RABADON_LENS_DIR** (line 1935) — for lens config\n- **USER** (line 638) — for ledger_line() events\n- **RABADON_MOVES_STRICT** (line 1252) — for move chain validation\n\n**FILES READ ON EVERY HOOK (per-request):**\n- State machine's shared file: `<cwd>/.rabadon/state.json` (line 2481-2482, State::load())\n- Session file: `<cwd>/.rabadon/sessions/<sessKey>.json` (line 2483)\n- Move log: `<cwd>/.rabadon/sessions/<sessKey>.moves.bin` (line 2486, State::load_moves())\n- Fingerprint log: `<cwd>/.rabadon/sessions/<sessKey>.fp.bin` (line 2486)\n- Guard file: wherever `guard_path_for()` finds it (line 2780)\n- Budget file: `.rabadon/budget.json` (line 4081)\n- Transcript file: path from event (line 4088-4091)\n- Net verdict: `.rabadon/net.json` (line 4350)\n\n**PROCESS-GLOBAL STATE @ startup (line 61-72):**\n- `g_mode` (line 61) — MODE_SILENT/MODE_ENFORCE/MODE_WATCH — resolved once per process at lines 2639-2645, never changes\n- `g_dialect` (line 65) — dialect (CLAUDE/CURSOR/etc) — set once at line 2565, never changes\n- `g_self` (line 68) — argv[0] for logging\n\n---\n\n### 4. SIDE EFFECTS ON HOOK PATH (writes)\n\n**Ledger appends (hash-chained, tamper-evident):**\n- **native/chain.h**: `rbchain::append(spoolPath, body)` called by:\n  - `em.emit()` (line 742) on every event emission — **multiple calls per hook** (CHECK_FAIL, STOP, WOULD_BLOCK, INJECT, STEP_START, etc.)\n  - `ledger_line()` (line 646) for CLI-triggered events (--wrong, MODE changes)\n- **Spool location:** `$RABADON_DIR/spool/<YYYY-MM-DD>.jsonl` (line 2717, 637)\n\n**State file writes (session + shared):**\n- **line 2733** `StateFlushGuard stt_flush(stt)` — guard object that calls `stt.save()` on any exit\n- **line 4655** explicit `stt.save()` before allow path\n- **line 4029, 4062, 4098** explicit saves before block/would-block exits\n- `stt.save()` (line 1550+) — writes `<cwd>/.rabadon/state.json` (merged with other sessions' updates) and `<cwd>/.rabadon/sessions/<sessKey>.json`\n\n**Move ring appends:**\n- **line 2831** `stt.append_move(*open_move)` — appends binary record to `<cwd>/.rabadon/sessions/<sessKey>.moves.bin` (native/gate.cpp:1267-1298)\n- **line 2839** `rbsem::store()` — semantic fingerprints to `.fp.bin`\n\n**Socket writes (to rabadon watch):**\n- **line 2725** `em.open_sock()` opens AF_UNIX socket at `$RABADON_DIR/rabadon.sock` (line 2718)\n- **line 743** every `em.emit()` writes the ledger line + newline to socket (non-blocking, EPIPE ignored)\n\n**Directory creates:**\n- **line 2707-2708** mkdir `$RABADON_DIR` and `$RABADON_DIR/spool`\n- **line 2729** mkdir `<cwd>/.rabadon`\n- **line 2735** mkdir `<cwd>/.rabadon/sessions`\n\n**DAEMON CORRECTNESS ISSUE:** All writes reference `cwd` and per-request state (session, moves, budget, transcript). A long-lived daemon with **different cwd** would write ledger/spool files to the **same `$RABADON_DIR`** but session/move files to **its own cwd**, creating split state. The daemon MUST either:\n1. Accept cwd per-request and switch working directory (unsafe, breaks fd paths), OR\n2. Accept **absolute paths** for all file references from the request\n\n---\n\n### 5. open_sock() AF_UNIX CLIENT to rabadon watch (lines 714-724)\n\n**Socket code (native/gate.cpp:714-724):**\n```cpp\nvoid open_sock() {\n  sockFd = socket(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0);\n  if (sockFd < 0) return;\n  fcntl(sockFd, F_SETFL, O_NONBLOCK);\n  struct sockaddr_un addr; memset(&addr, 0, sizeof(addr));\n  addr.sun_family = AF_UNIX;\n  strncpy(addr.sun_path, sockPath.c_str(), sizeof(addr.sun_path) - 1);\n  if (connect(sockFd, (struct sockaddr*)&addr, sizeof(addr)) < 0 && errno != EINPROGRESS) {\n    close(sockFd); sockFd = -1;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Socket path computation (line 2718):**\n- `em.sockPath = rdir + \"/rabadon.sock\";` where `rdir = rabadon_home()` (line 2706)\n- `rabadon_home()` → `rbpath::rabadon_dir()` (line 189) — uses env RABADON_DIR or `~/.rabadon`\n\n**Failure handling (line 721-723):**\n- If connect fails with errno != EINPROGRESS → close socket, set `sockFd = -1`\n- Silently fails; no exit, no block, gate continues\n- Writes to socket are best-effort (line 743): `write(sockFd, ...)` result is discarded\n\n**Emit to socket (line 743):**\n- `if (sockFd >= 0) { ssize_t r = write(...); (void)r; }` — non-blocking, EPIPE ignored (line 2128 SIGPIPE ignored)\n- Socket receives ledger lines as written to spool (chain.h::append output)\n\n---\n\n### 6. EXPENSIVE STARTUP WORK (Things daemon caches once)\n\n**None intrinsic to gate.cpp.** All parsing is on-demand:\n\n- **guard.json parsing:** done per-hook call at line 2780-2781; calls `parse_rules()` from rules.h which scans the raw JSON string (no compilation or pre-build)\n- **Regex compilation:** deferred to the moment a rule is matched; `std::regex(r.pattern)` in rules.h (called by `rbrules::judge_command()` at line 4161, not pre-compiled)\n- **State files:** read fresh on every hook (line 2738), but moves are read as binary blobs (line 1210-1263) in O(1) time (fixed ring buffer)\n- **No global fixture tables or lookup structures built at startup**\n\n**However, a daemon would cache once:**\n- `RABADON_DIR` resolution (env or `~/.rabadon`)\n- Machine-level mode file path (`$RABADON_DIR/mode`)\n- Socket path (`$RABADON_DIR/rabadon.sock`)\n- User name for ledger (USER env)\n- Binary paths (self_dir())\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY FOR DAEMON DESIGN\n\nThe daemon MUST accept per-request:\n- Hook event JSON (stdin mimics Claude Code)\n- `cwd` (implied or explicit in hook event)\n- All per-session/per-project files read fresh (no caching of state.json, budget.json, etc.)\n\nThe daemon can cache once:\n- Socket path (`$RABADON_DIR/rabadon.sock`)\n- Mode file locations\n- Spool directory path\n\n**Critical constraint:** All file writes (state, moves, ledger) reference `cwd`. The daemon must receive **complete hook event JSON with all paths resolved** or accept cwd explicitly and make all file paths absolute before accepting requests.\n\n**Exit protocol:** \n- 0 = ALLOW (stdout may contain hookSpecificOutput JSON for PreToolUse)\n- 2 = BLOCK enforce mode (stdout contains permission deny JSON for Cursor, or empty for Claude Code which checks exit code)"}],"totalDurationMs":122283,"totalTokens":62260,"totalToolUseCount":32,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":57954,"output_tokens":4091,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":210},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":4091,"cache_read_input_tokens":57954,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":210,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":14,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":18,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
