{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FQwRsxvELVayf2UD6d1Tdg","type":"tool_result","content":"rc=1\n\n== GOAL 1 — the daemon and the thin client exist at all\nPASS  1a rabadon-gated exists and is executable\nPASS  1b native/gated.cpp binds and listens on a unix socket (a daemon, not a one-shot)\nPASS  1c a thin client path referencing the daemon socket exists (native/gated_client.h)\n\n== GOAL 2 — with the daemon up, the gate's median is under 1 ms (in-process)\nFAIL  2a rabadon-gated did not produce a listening socket at /var/folders/5b/s4fb775925l775xmnt2zt_mr0000gn/T/tmp.mNbSuWiruq/rabadon-gated.sock\n      \n./reports/R7/accept.sh: line 178: 61913 Terminated: 15          env HOME=\"$DH\" RABADON_DIR=\"$DH/.rabadon\" RABADON_GATED_SOCK=\"$SOCK\" \"$GATED\" > \"$W/gated.log\" 2>&1\nFAIL  2b the < 1 ms median was NOT measured: no daemon to measure with\n      ceiling is 1000 us in-process; the instrument is the R1.3 probe (header)\nFAIL  2c the residual length dependence was NOT re-measured under the daemon\n      R1.3 closed at 3.5-4.9% under a 10% ceiling with process spawn IN the\n      denominator; the daemon removes spawn, so the same absolute cost reads as\n      a LARGER percentage. The plan requires R7 to re-read it. Unread today.\n\n== GOAL 3 — with the daemon down, behaviour is byte-identical to today\nFAIL  3-[echo hello world] behaviour diverges when the daemon is down — this is not fail-SAME\n      3,4c3,4\n      < {\"v\":1,\"seq\":1,\"ts\":T,\"run\":\"ng-68589448-61926\",\"pipe\":\"p.fKvHk1:session\",\"ev\":\"STEP_START\",\"sess\":\"s7\",\"step\":\"bash: echo hello world\",\"prev\":\"genesis\"}\n      < 7a48429b0d2c6574935b55cf54d6a6b145358ddfedf14b056953343119d3b012 1\n      ---\n      > {\"v\":1,\"seq\":1,\"ts\":T,\"run\":\"ng-68589483-61942\",\"pipe\":\"p.XQyK6D:session\",\"ev\":\"STEP_START\",\"sess\":\"s7\",\"step\":\"bash: echo hello world\",\"prev\":\"genesis\"}\n      > a76918903e9e5f137db4795944ab9c8a4667b